      \"line\": 5,\n      \"span\": \"Closest approach to Uranus took place at 17:59 UT on January 24, 1986, at a range of about 50,640 kilometers (81,500 miles)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 2 discovered 11 new moons\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The new moons discovered by Voyager 2 were given names such as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"given names such as Puck, Portia, Juliet, Cressida, Rosalind, Belinda, Desdemona, Cordelia, Ophelia, and Bianca\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"A naming tradition for the moons was begun in 1787.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"continuing a naming tradition begun in 1787\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 discovered three new rings in addition to the eight older rings of Uranus.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"three new rings in addition to the eight older rings\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus has a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"a magnetic field tilted at 66 degrees off-axis and off-center\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere are as high as 450 km/h (72,400 meters per hour).\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"The spacecraft found wind speeds in Uranus' atmosphere as high as 450 km/h (72,400 meters per hour)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"There is evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface of Uranus.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"found evidence of a boiling lake of water some 479 miles (900 kilometers) below the top cloud surface\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus' rings are extremely variable in thickness and transparency.\",\n      \"line\": 7,\n      \"span\": \"Its rings were found to be extremely variable in thickness and transparency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 returned photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, and Umbriel, among other smaller moons of Uranus.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"Voyager 2 also returned spectacular photos of Miranda, Oberon, Ariel, and Umbriel, among other smaller moons of Uranus\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Voyager 2 flew by Miranda at a range of 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers) and this was its closest approach to any object in its travels so far.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"In flying by Miranda at a range of only 17,560 miles (28,260 kilometers), the spacecraft came closest to any object so far in its nearly century-long travels\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"Uranus appeared generally featureless.\",\n      \"line\": 9,\n      \"span\": \"Uranus itself appeared generally featureless\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"text\": \"The Challenger accident killed seven crew members during their space shuttle launch on January 28, 1986.\",\n      \"line\": 11,\n      \"span\": \"the tragic Challenger accident that killed seven crew members during their space shuttle launch on January 28, 1986\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","ttft_ms":89114,"type":"result","duration_ms":96726,"uuid":"f8980e9c-6645-42a5-a809-f8038ae71060","ttft_stream_ms":709,"time_to_request_ms":115,"first_content_frame_ms":709,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
